@rule double
X t-day THE FIRST DAY.
T __MORNING PRAYER.__
T PSAL. i. __Beatus vir, qui non abiit.__
I BLESSED is the man that hath not walk-
  ed in the counsel of the ungodly, nor
  stood in the way of sinners: and hath not sat
  in the seat of the scornful;
P 2 But his delight is in the law of the Lord:
  and in his law will he exercise himself day and
  night.
P 3 And he shall be like a tree planted by the
  water-side: that will bring forth his fruit in
  due season.
P 4 His leaf also shall not wither: and look,
  whatsoever he doeth, it shall prosper.
P 5 As for the ungodly, it is not so with them:
  but they are like the chaff which the wind
  scattereth away from the face of the earth.
f X | 6 Therefore
